<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>(a) Write <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 0 \\ 5 \\ 1 \end{array}\right)}</m> in terms of <m>\mathbf{i}</m>, <m>\mathbf{j}</m> and <m>\mathbf{k}</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="15" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Write <m>{6 \mathbf{i}+7 \mathbf{k}}</m> as a column vector.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>A column <m>\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \\ z \end{pmatrix}</m> is <m>x\mathbf{i} + y\mathbf{j} + z\mathbf{k}</m>: each unit vector is one step along an axis. A zero component is left out of the i, j, k form, but kept as 0 in a column.</p><p>(a) <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 0 \\ 5 \\ 1 \end{array}\right)} = {5 \mathbf{j}+\mathbf{k}}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>{6 \mathbf{i}+7 \mathbf{k}} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 6 \\ 0 \\ 7 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>5 \mathbf{j}+\mathbf{k}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 6 \\ 0 \\ 7 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>